Ticket #4471 is marked **known**: one issue, one fix queued — the parser reads dates month
first, and our tenants write the day first. I went through all 412 reports merged into it.
That is not what they show.

<Callout>
Not one issue. The 412 reports hold **three problems**. Each one now has its own ticket.
</Callout>

## What the 412 reports hold

<SplitTable ticket={4471} />

## Why the merge missed it

- The desk merges on the subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
  Every one of these problems lands in a subject like "wrong day", so they all merged into one ticket.
- The intake tag (`meta.intakeTag`) is a guess from the reporter's browser. The true cause
  depends on the tenant: their locale and their booking form (`causes.ts`). The two disagree
  on 38 of these reports — 23 tagged `hint` are the parser bug, 15 tagged `parser` are the hint bug.
- The export itself pages with overlap: 15 report ids appear twice. One id, one report
  (`uniqueById`): 427 entries, 412 reports.

## The one-day moves, read closer

Five reports the desk read as one-day moves sit in `desk-notes.json`. Three are dates one
day off (R-41202, R-41209, R-41620). One is not a day move at all: R-41344 is the same
meeting shown on two days in two cities — a timezone render. R-41344 and R-41236 (an invite
that arrived before its booking) are flagged in the ticket for engineering to look at separately.

## Update — the desk closed #4471 (05 Oct)

Engineering update: **parser** — fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`).
**hint** — won't fix: the booking-v3 form is retired. The one-day moves stay flagged in their
ticket for engineering (R-41344 timezone, R-41236 ordering).

